% formalizes: claim:lib-6d
% claim: An uncollected hold lapses and the copy passes to the next hold, or to the shelf
% says: If they do not collect it, the hold lapses and the copy passes to the next in line, or to the shelf if there is no one.
% fidelity: strained — a change of state over time (the hold lapses, the copy passes on); stated as what holds once the week is up.
lapsed(H) :- set_aside_on(_, H, D1), one_week_after(D1, D0), today(N), D0 < N, not collected(H).
